WEBVTT

NOTE DATOM How it works film. Generated by scripts/howitworks-captions.ts from howitworks/narration.json; do not hand edit.

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.670
AI cannot be fully trusted in science: it predicts a likely answer, and it can cite a source that does not exist.

2
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.330
That is where verification comes in, and this is how a DATOM record is made.

3
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.270
Every record is a receipt for one claim.

4
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.710
It holds the claim stated exactly, a verdict, an evidence grade, and every source they rest on.

5
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.280
The verdict says which way the evidence points, and nothing more.

6
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.170
Each study is weighted for its design, its size, and how directly it tests the claim.

7
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:38.110
Findings from the same paper or the same authors are grouped, so the evidence gives a range, not a single number.

8
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:47.090
A claim is Supported only when the bottom of that range is at 55% or above, and Unsupported only when the top is at 45% or below.

9
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.250
Anything between is Contested: the evidence does not settle it.

10
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.030
One test comes before all of these: whether there is enough evidence to say anything.

11
00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.410
If there is not, the record says Insufficient record, and states no direction at all.

12
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:08.830
The evidence grade says how solid the ground is, from A to F, judged against the strongest kind of study the question allows.

13
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.530
It is a letter, never a percentage, because a percentage would read as the chance the claim is true.

14
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:19.340
Every source is listed on the record, with an identifier you can follow to the paper.

15
00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.290
A record whose citations cannot be checked does not publish.

16
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.140
The result is free of bias: only the evidence moves it.

17
00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.910
Every record says who commissioned it, or that no one did.

18
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.430
What the public believes about a claim carries no weight.

19
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:42.470
It is stored where scoring cannot read it, and the scoring is run twice, with it and without it: the results must match to the last bit.

20
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.810
A published record is added to, never rewritten.

21
00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:53.070
When the evidence changes it, the change is dated and its reason named, and the earlier version stays in the record's history.

22
00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.990
Claims arrive three ways: chosen by DATOM, asked for by readers, or commissioned.

23
00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:06.290
Commissioned work stays private until the customer chooses to publish, but a customer cannot keep a claim from being checked when readers ask for it.

24
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.930
DATOM does not decide what is true.

25
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:14.970
The record shows which way the evidence points and how solid the ground is, and the decision stays yours.

26
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.010
DATOM.

27
00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.960
Science, verified.

28
00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:18.940
For everyone.
